{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"In **ResStock 2025 Release 1**:\n\n- **Heating setpoints range from 55°F to 80°F**, with discrete options of 55, 60, 62, 65, 67, 68, 70, 72, 75, 76, 78, and 80°F. See Table 99 in the [2025.1 Technical Reference Guide, p. 136](https://natlabrockies.github.io/ResStock.github.io/assets/trd/ResStockTechnicalReferenceGuide_2025_1.pdf#page=136).\n- **The distribution is derived from the U.S. EIA’s 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS)** and varies by climate zone, building type, HVAC type, and tenure. See [HVAC Load Flexibility report, Section 2, p. 8](https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/93846.pdf#page=16).\n- **A 55°F setpoint represents a vacant dwelling**, with heating maintained to prevent pipes from freezing. See the footnote to Figure 1 in the [same report, p. 8](https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/93846.pdf#page=16)."}}
